<title>UK: Scottish funds rose to new record in 1995.</title>
<headline>Scottish funds rose to new record in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>EDINBURGH 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scottish funds under management rose 25 percent last year to a record 170 billion stg, according to a survey by the business lobby group Scottish Financial Enterprise (SFE).</p>
<p>Assurance/insurance companies, which manage nearly three-quarters of the total, registered an increase of 28 percent, while specialist fund managers saw a rise of 14 percent.</p>
<p>Other groups, such as banks and stockbrokers, had an increase of almost 33 percent, the SFE said.</p>
<p>-- Bill Magee, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770</p>
</text>
